    "lawCode": "Add §170-b, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3088\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to prohibiting state\nagencies from offering loans to their employees\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nProhibits state agencies from issuing interest free loans to\nemployees, unless authorized by state and federal law.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nA new Section 170-a is added to the Executive Law which would prohibit\nany state agency from offering loans to employees.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIt was reported in the fall of 1993 that the Job Development Authority\n(JDA) had been making interest free loans to its top executives.\nApproximately $87,000 of JDA funds were \"lent\" to about two dozen\nauthority employees including more than $20,000 to the JDA President\nwho used the money to payoff her credit card bills, one of which was\nfor her airfare for a personal visit to France. The JDA funds are\nsupposed to be used to assist the state's businesses to maintain and\ncreate jobs. This bill will prevent this practice for all state\nagencies.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2001-2002: A.2697/S.1508 (Senate Rules Committee)\n2003-2004: A.188 - Passed Assembly\n2005-2006: A.1348 - Passed Assembly\n2007-2008: A.371 - Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nNinety days after it shall become law.\n",
